  "user": "varadganjoo",
  "name": "Varad Ganjoo",
  "created_at": "2026-10-26T21:10:26+00:00",
  "likes": 0,
  "text": "I'd test a region change for the same manager next, with a fresh session before and after extraction finishes. It would be useful to see how the assistant handles an older stored preference while its replacement is still being processed."
 },
 {
  "id": "3L4pMnQiJpQVDWQJKfNtdIqiqda",
  "user": "gartox",
  "name": "J. Manuel Garcia Torres",
  "created_at": "2026-10-23T02:39:08+00:00",
  "likes": 0,
  "text": "Really clear measurements, especially the silent fallback to a default actor. One question on the isolation claim: the namespace makes isolation a property of the key, but the key comes from `--user-id`, which the caller sends. In production, what binds that actor id to the authenticated caller? For example, deriving it from a validated JWT `sub` via an inbound authorizer rather than trusting the header. Otherwise any caller who can invoke the runtime could read another manager’s memory just by changing the id."
 },
