  "likes": 2,
  "text": "Baking isolation directly into the namespace key space (`/episodes/{actorId}/`) rather than relying on application-level filtering is such an elegant multi-tenant architecture pattern.\n\nThe asynchronous extraction latency measurements are the real eye-opener here—quantifying that preference extraction took 255s while episodic reflection required ~17 minutes (1,022s) completely changes how you architect integration test timeouts and poll cycles. Also appreciate the hard-won gotcha callouts, especially the 33-character minimum on `runtimeSessionId` and the exact header mapping for `--user-id`. Measuring `RetrieveMemoryRecords` traces at ~260–350 ms before model execution proves that pre-retrieval prompt injection remains fast across multiple namespaces. Outstanding practical write-up!"
 },
